# Recovery-mode init. Lands at the root of the recovery ramdisk, where init
# picks it up as /init.recovery.${ro.hardware}.rc (ro.hardware = mt6789 from
# the dtb cmdline).
#
# Without this the recovery ramdisk has no USB gadget configuration, so
# `adb sideload` never enumerates.
#
# Derived from stock's copy in ADVAN_6781_S34NF2_V4.0_20250304 vendor_boot
# (vendor_ramdisk00, zip-CRC-chained; sha256 d8fc8d253d7aa08d...), with three
# removals, each a reference to something that does not exist here:
#   * import /init.recovery.project.rc -- not in stock's vendor ramdisk.
#   * `on boot` exec of /system/bin/mtk_plpath_utils (builds the legacy
#     /dev/block/platform/... link tree) -- this build installs no such
#     binary into recovery; everything here uses /dev/block/by-name, which
#     ueventd creates.
#   * `on late-init` exec of /vendor/bin/linkud in u:r:storage_turbo:s0
#     (a Prize "storage turbo" addition) -- stock's vendor partition ships no
#     linkud, and this tree's policy has no storage_turbo domain.
# The first two are the same removals the S666LN tree made to its stock copy.

on init
    setprop sys.usb.configfs 1
    setprop sys.usb.controller "musb-hdrc"
    setprop sys.usb.ffs.aio_compat 0

on fs && property:ro.debuggable=0
    # Tell the charger whether USB is a CDP or an SDP port. Without this the
    # port is treated as charging-only and waits for USB activation that
    # never comes.
    write /sys/class/udc/musb-hdrc/device/cmode 2
    start adbd
